# ─── Docker runtime files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing under data/ is application code: it is the developer's pantry, their
# tokens and their caches. `COPY .` used to bake all of it into the image —
# including data/mealie/docker-compose.yml, which holds the Mealie admin
# password in clear text. Everything mutable is listed here.
#
# Pattern semantics worth remembering: a pattern without a slash matches only at
# the context root, so `*.apk` and `__pycache__/` did nothing for nested files
# and a 6.7 MB local APK and a .pyc still landed in the image. Anything that has
# to match at any depth is written `**/…` below.
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/*.db.bak*
data/backups/
data/rate_limits/
data/*.log*
data/*.crt
data/*.pem
data/mealie/
data/*_cache.json
data/weather_cache_*.json
data/api_pairing.json
data/bring_token.json
data/bring_catalog.json
data/bring_migrate_ts.json
data/anomaly_dismissed.json
data/ai_usage.json
data/classify_daily.json
data/shopping_spend.json
data/backup_last_ts.json
data/audit_finished_missing.json
data/reported_issue_fps.json

# ─── Local artefacts and secrets (all gitignored, none needed at runtime) ────
# These reached the image through the pattern trap described above.
**/*.apk
# signing keystores (evershelf-health-bridge/evershelf.jks)
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/keystore.properties
# local certificates and keys (ca.crt at the repo root)
**/*.crt
**/*.pem
**/*.key
# python bytecode
**/*.pyc
**/__pycache__/
# hand-made copies of logos and other assets (assets/img/logo/*_backup.png)
**/*_backup.*
# application logs: runtime data, not code (logs/evershelf_YYYY-MM-DD_HH.log)
logs/*.log*

# Shipped on purpose: the deny rules, the directory placeholder and the source
# data of the seasonal feature. Re-included after every pattern above so a
# broader rule cannot silently drop them.
!data/.htaccess
!data/.gitkeep
!data/seasonal_produce_it.json

# ─── Development-only trees that `COPY .` used to drag in ────────────────────
mcp-server/node_modules/
evershelf-kiosk/
screenshots/
todo/

# The MiniLM weights are gitignored: the Dockerfile fetches them itself, so the
# published image and a locally built one finally contain the same files.
assets/vendor/transformers/Xenova/

# releases/ stays in the context: api/index.php `getKioskUpdate()` answers with
# releases/kiosk-version.json. Put your own APK there via a bind mount — *.apk is
# ignored on purpose, so an image never carries one of your local builds.

# ─── Config (mounted as volume) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.env

# ─── Git ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore

# ─── Docs and build files (not needed in the container) ──────────────────────
# None of these are read at runtime, and serving them from the web root is free
# information for a scanner: /Dockerfile, /CHANGELOG.md.
# docker/ must stay in the context: the Dockerfile COPYs php-evershelf.ini and
# apache-evershelf.conf from it.
**/*.md
docs/
LICENSE
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.github/
.cursorignore

# ─── IDE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

